# HELUT Architecture Rules
- DOMAIN: We are implementing TFHE Programmable Bootstrapping (PBS) using `MPSGraph`.
- SUBVERSION: We are NOT using standard cryptographic libraries. We are mapping polynomial multiplications over $\mathbb{Z}_{2^{32}}[X]/(X^N+1)$ into dense Matrix-Vector multiplications.
- DATA TYPES: TFHE torus arithmetic relies on exact modulo $2^{32}$ wrapping. All tensors in `MPSGraph` must use `MPSDataType.uInt32`. Do not use floats.
- MEMORY: Rely on `MTLBuffer` zero-copy bridging. We will expand key polynomials into explicit Negacyclic Toeplitz matrices (size $N \times N$) in memory to force the hardware to evaluate them via dense linear algebra.
- PROHIBITION: Do not import any Machine Learning dependencies other than `Metal` and `MetalPerformanceShadersGraph`.
